# Mobbin first

Before adding or restyling section/card headers, run **Mobbin** `search_screens` (web):

- Mercury: `Mercury dashboard card header`, `Mercury money movement transactions`
- Accounting peers: `QuickBooks profit loss dashboard`, `fintech tax breakdown web`

Prefer **Mercury** for Freelax dashboard/tax/compliance. Use QuickBooks/Bonsai only for P&L *content* patterns, not their ALL-CAPS widget chrome.

# Three levels (do not mix roles)

| Level | Token / component | Use for | Shell |
|-------|-------------------|---------|--------|
| **Page** | `PageHeader` (serif `text-2xl`) | Page name + **one** subtitle (tax year, date, entity) | Outside cards |
| **Section** | `sectionTitle` on `h2` | Named block: Profit & Loss, VAT position, MTD | See shells below |
| **Eyebrow** | `cardLabel` on `p` | Optional group label only: At a glance, Suggested next steps | No `h2`; never duplicate a section title |

Do **not** add a fourth hero title (`text-lg`) on the same page unless it replaces the page subtitle.

# Section shells — pick one per surface

## A. Flat money card (Mercury default — dashboard, tax, compliance)

Use `SectionCard` with `variant="flat"` and optional `action`:

```tsx
<SectionCard
  variant="flat"
  title="VAT position"
  action={<Link className={buttonVariants({ intent: 'secondary', size: 'sm' })} href="…">VAT Returns →</Link>}
  bodyClassName="py-1"
>
  {/* hero metric, breakdown, chart */}
</SectionCard>
```

- Title **without** tax year in the card (year lives in `PageHeader` subtitle).
- **One** header CTA — `Button` / `Link` + `secondary` `sm`. No footer duplicate links to the same destination.
- Optional in-card footer: quiet `View →` text link (Mercury), not a second paragraph of instructions.

## B. Section band above a grid (Mercury — Money movement, Transactions)

For a **group** of cards, not a single card:

```tsx
<div className="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-3">
  <h2 className={sectionTitle}>Important dates</h2>
  <Link className="text-sm text-brand-primary …">View all →</Link>
</div>
<div className="grid …">{/* cards */}</div>
```

Spacing separates the band from the grid (`mb-3` / `gap-8` between bands). No sunken header strip.

## C. Sunken header (`SectionCard`) — settings & dense breakdown only

Use for **long label/value tables** (P&L rows, NI breakdown, settings tabs) where the body is mostly `BreakdownRow` lines.

Do **not** use sunken `SectionCard` headers next to flat Mercury-style cards on the **same row** (e.g. VAT flat + P&L sunken). Prefer migrating breakdown blocks to a flat header variant when touching that page.

# Mercury patterns to copy

- Card title top-left; actions top-right on **same row**.
- Section labels between card groups; **whitespace** > extra chrome.
- Summary stat cards: small label above big number (`cardLabel` + `serifStat`), not a second `sectionTitle`.

# Anti-patterns

- Gray sunken header + inline white-body title on the same viewport band.
- `sectionTitle` + `cardLabel` for the same block.
- Repeating `— 2026/27` on every card when the page subtitle already has the tax year.
- Text-link “Connect HMRC” in the card footer when the header already has `Connect HMRC →`.
- QuickBooks-style ALL-CAPS widget titles on Freelax UI.
